## Maximus Technologies — Week 4 Workbook (Raymond)

**Cohort**: AI powered Developer Learning  
**Trainee**: Raymond  
**Week**: 4  
**Dates**: Mon 10 Nov 2025 → Fri 14 Nov 2025 (Africa/Kampala)  
**Version**: v1.0  
**Mentor**: Paul / Maximus Technologies Mentors

### How to Use This Workbook
- **Source of truth** for Week 4 scope, acceptance bars, artifacts, and daily checklists.
- **Workflow**: create/claim a GitHub Issue (add to Project) → branch → PR → Release/Pages → Review Packet.
- **Submission**: one capstone PR by Friday EOD aggregating the week’s work with all evidence.

### Week 4 Theme
Spec-driven product slices, Figma integration, and publishing. Design in Figma, slice features into reviewable increments, and ship them with Releases + Pages for quick verification.


## Week 4 Outcomes (Go/No Go Gate — all must be true by Fri EOD, 14 Nov 2025)
- [ ] Day 0 finishers from Week 3 completed with proof screenshots (see Day 0).
- [ ] Figma integration: component inventory + 1–2 user flows; link in PR + README.
- [ ] Three product slices shipped to development behind CI gates; Spec Kit (/specify → /plan → /tasks) updated per slice.
- [ ] Tests & coverage: unit (CLI+UI) + Playwright smoke per slice. Targets:
  - [ ] UI ≥ 80% statements overall (≥ 50% per changed module minimum).
  - [ ] CLI ≥ 60% statements aggregate.
- [ ] Accessibility: labeled form controls; inline errors; keyboard focus order; a11y smoke (axe or equivalent) in CI.
- [ ] Reviewability:
  - [ ] GitHub Release published with the Week 4 Review Packet (coverage HTML + Playwright report + review.md).
  - [ ] GitHub Pages (or Cloud Run preview) updated for Coverage Index and UI demo links.
  - [ ] README has “How to review me (Week 4)” with Release + Pages links.
- [ ] GitHub Projects discipline: Issues ↔ PRs auto-linked (`Closes #123`), branches follow `feature/gh-123-scope`, cards appear on Project board. Screenshots in PR.
- [ ] Branch protection on `development` enforced; all checks required; screenshot in PR.
- [ ] Capstone PR merged with Coverage Table (CLI + UI), Release/Pages links, Figma link, and proof screenshots.


