## Technical Requirements & Patterns

### Figma → Code
- Component inventory drives code components; map tokens to Tailwind theme (colors/spacing/radii/shadows).
- Export SVGs/PNG as needed; prefer CSS for simple icons.
- Keep names consistent (e.g., `Button/Primary`, `Badge/High`).

### Spec Kit discipline
- `/specify`: problem, scope boundaries, acceptance rules.
- `/plan`: UI flows, state shapes, test plan (unit + e2e + a11y), risks.
- `/tasks`: granular steps; link each task to commits/PRs.

### Testing & a11y
- Unit: Vitest + RTL; table driven; inject clock/seed.
- e2e smoke: Playwright with deterministic fixtures; tag `@smoke`.
- a11y: an axe (or equivalent) smoke test per route; labeled controls; focus management.
- Coverage: collect CLI + UI separately; export HTML to `review-artifacts/` with an index.

### CI & Publishing
- Branch protection on `development`: require lint, unit, e2e, a11y, packet build.
- Releases: every capstone PR publishes a Packet ZIP.
- Pages/Preview: Coverage Index + demo links surfaced in README’s review box.

### PR Discipline
- Branch: `feature/gh-<issue>-short-scope` (e.g., `feature/gh-123-expenses-upload`)
- Title: `feat(scope): short description (#123)`
- Body: What changed / How I tested (real outputs) / Artifacts (Release & Pages links + Figma) / Coverage Table / Screenshots (Project card + branch protection) / Linked issues.


## Deliverables (What to Submit)
- [ ] Screenshots: Release asset, Pages URL, Figma link in README, GitHub Project card & Issue link proof, branch protection rules.
- [ ] Review Packet: Coverage HTML (CLI + UI), Playwright report, `review.md`.
- [ ] Capstone PR merged with Coverage Table and artifact links.


## Mentor Review Rubric (Pass/Revise)

### 1) Discipline (Spec Kit, GitHub Projects & Issues, PR hygiene)
- **Pass**: Issues → branches → PRs; screenshots in PR; Spec Kit updated per slice.
- **Revise**: Missing links/screens; ad hoc branches; stale specs.

### 2) Correctness (UI parity & rules)
- **Pass**: UI mirrors CLI; helpful inline errors; deterministic flows; a11y considered.
- **Revise**: Happy path only; mismatched validation; poor a11y.

### 3) Tests & Coverage
- **Pass**: Targets met (UI ≥ 80% overall / ≥ 50% changed); deterministic unit + e2e + a11y smoke.
- **Revise**: Targets missed; lack of smokes; brittle tests.

### 4) Artifacts & Reviewability
- **Pass**: Release with Packet; Pages/preview live; README review box current.
- **Revise**: Missing Release/Pages; artifacts hard to find.


## Appendices

### A) README — “How to review me (Week 4)” — sample

```markdown
## How to review this project (Week 4)

- **Release (Packet)**: Download the Review Packet ZIP from the latest Release → open `review-artifacts/index.html`.
- **Live demo**: Visit GitHub Pages for the UI demo (links below each slice).
- **What changed**: See the Week 4 Capstone PR body for coverage, screenshots, and links.
- **Design**: Figma link to component inventory and user flows.
```

### B) Playwright smoke — sample

```ts
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('@smoke expenses happy path', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto(process.env.UI_BASE_URL!);
  await page.getByLabel('Upload CSV').setInputFiles('fixtures/expenses.csv');
  await page.getByLabel('Month').selectOption('March');
  await page.getByLabel('Category').selectOption('Utilities');
  await expect(page.getByTestId('total')).toHaveText('$120.50');
});
```

### C) Coverage commands — reminder

```bash
pnpm test -- --coverage
pnpm exec playwright test --project=chromium --grep @smoke
xdg-open coverage/index.html || open coverage/index.html
```

